(* fs-records-b2s C4, security result (abstraction witness), (K_s, K_r,
   T_max) = (2, 3, 2), any Beacon pins: a Server peer accepts a frame above
   T_max only if the attacker holds the identity secret of the peer, so the
   far branch never fires for a peer registered by an honest Beacon, whose
   sends stay at or below T_max.  Run in the process in which the attacker
   chooses the pinned Server key and Server ID of every Beacon, with
   adversary-chosen record plaintexts and the fail-stop receive form
   (E21). *)
query s: bitstring, k: bitstring, kid: key_id, root: bitstring, t: nat;
  event(FsFarAccepted(beacon_to_server(), s, ed_public(k), kid, root, t)) ==> attacker(k).

process FsRecordsB2sMainAnyPin()
